stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> PENDING: Policy requires approval, insert row

    PENDING --> APPROVED: Finance approver decision
    PENDING --> REJECTED: Finance approver rejection
    PENDING --> EXPIRED: Expiry noticed during get / decide / consume

    APPROVED --> APPROVED: Current policy denies or audit write fails
    APPROVED --> EXPIRED: Expiry noticed before consumption
    APPROVED --> CONSUMED: Exact requester + operation digest, atomic consume

    CONSUMED --> [*]
    REJECTED --> [*]
    EXPIRED --> [*]

    note right of PENDING
        SQLite stores requester, digest, created/expiry times and status.
        CREATED / APPROVED / REJECTED / EXPIRED events are persisted
        with their state changes. Expiration is lazy, when state is read
        or changed.
    end note

    note right of CONSUMED
        CONSUMED state and event commit before the simulated handler runs.
        A process crash after consume can leave the operation unexecuted.
        this prototype has no transactional outbox or retry recovery.
    end note
